Keep the Go module replacements that identify the actual sources linked into a
binary. Go's normal build command records these with debug.Module.Replace.
rules_go v0.65.0 currently records only the original path, version and checksum.
Gazelle's archive_override can supply a REPO.bazel whose package metadata adds
the effective module's path, version and checksum as Go-specific PURL qualifiers.
Only packages reachable from the executable contribute records. This is needed
for the source-generated OBI receiver and the Avro fork in Collector v0.165.0.

